{
  "appPolicies" : {
    "eula" : "End User License Agreement (\"EULA\") for LiNGUiD\n\nThis End User License Agreement (\"EULA\") is a legal agreement between you (\"User\" or \"You\") and LiNGUiD LLC (\"Company,\" \"We,\" or \"Us\") for the use of the LiNGUiD mobile application (\"App\"), a social media platform designed to connect users for language learning and cultural exchange. By downloading, installing, accessing, or using the App, you agree to be bound by the terms of this EULA and our Community Guidelines, available at https://www.learnwithlinguid.com/community-guidelines. If you do not agree to these terms, do not download, install, or use the App.\n\n1. License Grant\nLiNGUiD LLC grants you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to use the App for personal, non-commercial purposes related to language learning and social interaction, on a single device, subject to the terms of this EULA and in accordance with the App's documentation and features.\n\n2. App Purpose and Usage\nThe App is a social media platform that enables users to connect, share language-related content (e.g., text, images, videos, or audio), participate in language learning activities (e.g., lessons, quizzes, or group chats), and engage in cultural exchange. You may use the App to create, share, and interact with content, connect with other language learners, and access features provided by LiNGUiD LLC.\n\n3. Eligibility\nYou must be at least 13 years old to use the App. If you are under 18, you represent that you have parental or guardian consent to use the App and agree to this EULA. By using the App, you confirm that you meet these eligibility requirements.\n\n4. User Content\nContent Ownership: You retain ownership of any content you create, upload, or share through the App (\"User Content\"), such as posts, comments, or media related to language learning. You are responsible for ensuring your User Content complies with this EULA and applicable laws.\nContent License: By posting User Content, you grant LiNGUiD LLC a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, sublicensable, and transferable license to use, reproduce, modify, distribute, display, and perform your User Content in connection with operating, promoting, and improving the App, including sharing it with other users as permitted by your privacy settings. This license ends when you delete your User Content or account, except for content shared with others that they have not deleted.\nContent Standards: User Content must not:\nViolate any laws or infringe on the rights of others (e.g., copyright, trademark, or privacy rights).\nContain hate speech, harassment, bullying, or discriminatory content.\nInclude explicit, violent, or otherwise inappropriate material.\nPromote illegal activities or harm to others.\nLiNGUiD LLC reserves the right to remove or restrict access to any User Content that violates this EULA or our Community Guidelines.\n\n5. Community Guidelines\nYou agree to follow our Community Guidelines, which promote a safe and respectful environment for language learning. These guidelines prohibit behaviors such as spamming, impersonation, or posting misleading content. Violations may result in content removal, account suspension, or termination.\n\n6. Restrictions\nYou may not:\n\nModify, reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the App, except as permitted by applicable law.\nCopy, distribute, sublicense, rent, lease, or transfer the App or its features to any third party.\nUse the App for unlawful purposes, to harass or harm others, or to disrupt the App's functionality.\nCreate multiple accounts to bypass restrictions, manipulate App features, or engage in fraudulent activity.\nUse automated tools (e.g., bots or scrapers) to access or collect data from the App without permission.\nRemove or alter any copyright, trademark, or other proprietary notices in the App.\n7. Ownership\nThe App and its content (excluding User Content) are licensed, not sold. LiNGUiD LLC and its licensors retain all right, title, and interest in the App, including all intellectual property rights. No ownership rights are transferred to you under this EULA.\n\n8. Account and Privacy\nAccount Creation: To access certain features, you must create an account with accurate information. You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and for all activities under your account.\nAccount Security: You must notify us immediately of any unauthorized use of your account. LiNGUiD LLC is not liable for losses caused by unauthorized access due to your failure to secure your account.\nPrivacy: Your use of the App is governed by our Privacy Policy, available at https://www.learnwithlinguid.com/privacy-policy, which explains how we collect, use, share, and protect your personal information.\n9. Subscriptions and Payments\nMonthly Subscription: Certain features of the App may be available only through a monthly subscription (\"Subscription\"). Your Subscription will automatically renew at the end of each monthly billing cycle unless you cancel it.\nCancellation: You may cancel your Subscription at any time through the app store settings on your device (e.g., Apple App Store or Google Play Store). Cancellation will take effect at the end of the current billing cycle, and you will retain access to the Subscription features until that time. We do not provide refunds or credits for any partial subscription periods.\nPricing: LiNGUiD LLC reserves the right to change the Subscription price with prior notice to you. Any price change will take effect in the next billing cycle.\n10. Updates and Modifications\nLiNGUiD LLC may release updates, patches, or new features for the App at its discretion. We may also modify or discontinue features or the entire App with or without notice. Updates are subject to this EULA unless otherwise specified. Continued use of the App after changes constitutes your acceptance of the updated terms.\n\n11. Third-Party Services\nThe App may integrate third-party services, such as analytics tools or external content providers. These services are subject to their own terms and privacy policies, and LiNGUiD LLC is not responsible for their operation or content.\n\n12. Termination\nThis EULA is effective until terminated. You may terminate it by deleting your account and uninstalling the App. LiNGUiD LLC may suspend or terminate your access to the App if you violate this EULA, our Community Guidelines, or engage in conduct that harms the App or its users. Upon termination, you must cease all use of the App and delete all copies in your possession. Provisions related to User Content licenses, disclaimers, and liability survive termination.\n\n13. Disclaimer of Warranties\nThe App is provided \"as is\" without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. LiNGUiD LLC does not guarantee that the App will be uninterrupted, error-free, secure, or free of harmful components. You use the App at your own risk.\n\n14. Limitation of Liability\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, LiNGUiD LLC, its affiliates, and licensors shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or any loss of profits, data, or use, arising out of or in connection with the App, even if advised of the possibility of such damages. In no event shall our total liability exceed the amount you paid, if any, to use the App.\n\n15. Indemnification\nYou agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless LiNGUiD LLC, its affiliates, officers, directors, employees, and agents from and against any and all claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses (including reasonable legal and accounting fees) arising out of or in any way connected with your access to or use of the App, your violation of this EULA, your User Content, or your infringement of any third-party right, including without limitation, any intellectual property or privacy right.\n\n16. Force Majeure\nLiNGUiD LLC shall not be liable for any delay or failure to perform any obligation under this EULA to the extent that the delay or failure is due to an event beyond our reasonable control, including but not limited to acts of God, war, natural disaster, terrorism, riot, embargoes, fire, strikes, lockouts, or governmental restrictions.\n\n17. Governing Law and Dispute Resolution\nThis EULA is governed by the laws of the State of Delaware, USA, without regard to its conflict of law principles. Any disputes arising under this EULA shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts in Wilmington, Delaware. You agree to attempt to resolve disputes informally with us before pursuing legal action.\n\n18. Severability\nIf any provision of this EULA is found to be invalid, illegal, or unenforceable by a court of competent jurisdiction, the remaining provisions of this EULA will remain in full force and effect.\n\n19. Waiver\nNo waiver of any term or condition of this EULA shall be deemed a further or continuing waiver of such term or any other term, and LiNGUiD LLC's failure to assert any right or provision under this EULA shall not constitute a waiver of such right or provision.\n\n20. Entire Agreement\nThis EULA, together with the Privacy Policy and Community Guidelines, constitutes the entire agreement between you and LiNGUiD LLC regarding the use of the App and supersedes any prior agreements or understandings, whether written or oral.\n\n21. Contact Information\nIf you have questions about this EULA, please contact LiNGUiD LLC at:\n\nEmail: julianoleary@learnwithlinguid.com\n\nBy using the App, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by this EULA and our Community Guidelines.",
